{
  "_meta": {
    "purpose": "Calibration corpus for core.waf_payload_analyzer (docs/waf_payload_analyzer.md Milestone C)",
    "updated": "2026-08-11",
    "design": [
      "The known_good half is the one that matters. A WAF payload classifier tuned only for recall looks excellent right up to the point analysts start ignoring it, and briefing 5 names alert fatigue as the failure this module exists to avoid.",
      "known_good is not 'safe traffic'. It is text that a WAF might flag or that an analyst might paste, which must NOT be called Malicious. Several entries deliberately contain SQL keywords, angle brackets, quotes and traversal-looking strings.",
      "expected is the verdict floor being asserted, not a prediction of the score. known_bad entries assert 'at least Suspicious'; known_good entries assert 'not Malicious'."
    ],
    "expected_semantics": {
      "known_bad": "must reach Suspicious or Malicious",
      "known_good": "must NOT reach Malicious; Unknown or Suspicious is acceptable, Unknown preferred"
    }
  },
